{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When you lend your neighbor</b> juxtaposed to tzara'at — to say that through this tzara'at comes: his fellow says to him, \"Lend me your vessel,\" and he says, \"I don't have it,\" and the next day nega'im come upon his house, and the priest commands, \"Empty the house,\" and everyone sees that he does have it:" "<b>(14)</b> You shall not oppress a hired worker. Juxtaposed to \"when you lend\" — to say: even if he owes you, do not say, \"I will detain him for my debt,\" but pay him his wages immediately and afterward collect your debt:" "<b>YHWH your</b> Elohim. And juxtaposed to it: \"you shall not oppress.\" To say: if one oppressed the poor, it is as though he oppressed HaShem, as it is written: \"He who is gracious to the poor lends to YHWH\" (Proverbs 19:17):"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:34.880151379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}